From ae78e98f533da37a2bb78b3ddcde44d8f8834be7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NayiemW <37852059+NayiemW@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 04:59:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Match the genesis issuance by the decoded key and cap it

Two follow-ups to patch 40.

1. TransferTransactionHandler.bootstrap() takes the genesis generator
key from the decoded genesis block, StateStore.getGenesisBlock().data.
generatorPublicKey, instead of the raw config string
genesisBlock.generatorPublicKey. That is the key
StateStore.setGenesisBlock() counts issued with, and the one the stored
transactions carry. The schema accepts hex in either case, so a
genesisBlock.json that writes the key in upper case is the same block
(same bytes, id and signature). In s1-ref-v1 the bootstrap then did not
recognise the issuance record and debited the generator by the whole
supply: -10000000000000000 on a devnet, while issued said
10000000000000000.

2. issued is at most 2^63 - 1. StateStore.setGenesisBlock() now
refuses, and stores nothing for, a genesis whose issuance items sum to
more than 2^63 - 1 ("The genesis block issues <n>, more than
2^63 - 1"). DatabaseInteraction.initialise() calls it as the last
genesis check, so the node terminates with "Invalid genesis block" and
exits with code 1, as patch 46 does for the other genesis rules. Each
item is a u64 on the wire and genesis items bypass the 2^63 - 1 schema
maximum, so the sum could exceed a u64 before. The limit is 2^63 - 1,
not 2^64 - 1, because StateSaver writes every balance as a signed
64-bit integer (writeBigInt64LE): a wallet holding 2^63 or more at
height 1 would make every saved-state write fail. No wallet can hold
more than issued at height 1 without another wallet going negative,
which patch 45 refuses, so the cap on issued caps every balance there.

Also in this commit: patches/tests/40-genesis-issuance.test.js gains an
app stub on its TransferTransactionHandler (3 lines, setup only). The
handler now reads the StateStore, which the stub lacked; the stub
returns the configured generator key, so test 40 checks exactly what
it did before. Test 40 still gives 19 passed on s1-ref-v1 and 10 failed
on the baseline b45369d7.

Checked on a running devnet node (with patch 45) whose genesisBlock.json
names the generator key in upper case: the bootstrap of s1-ref-v1 left
the generator at -10000000000000000 and patch 45 stopped the node with
"State Generation failed: Wallet with negative balance"; the bootstrap
here recognises the issuance record.

Test: patches/tests/49-genesis-issuance-key-and-limit.test.js (real
genesis blocks, a real StateStore). Upper-case key: the generator ends
at 0 and the sum of balances equals issued (base: -10000000000000000
and 0). Issuance of exactly 2^63 - 1 to one wallet is accepted, and the
real StateSaver writes that wallet (it cannot write a balance of 2^63).
Issuance of 2^63, in three items in a block that verifies, is refused
by setGenesisBlock and makes initialise() terminate and exit 1 (before
this patch: accepted). 2^64 - 1, which a u64 limit would accept, and
2^64 are refused with the new message.

Patch: 49
Consensus: yes
